WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.777 --> 00:00:02.437
Hey Joe, drag your foot, boy.

2
00:00:02.517 --> 00:00:03.811
Look what we got here.

3
00:00:04.097 --> 00:00:05.797
Hey, you want to drag, huh?

4
00:00:06.417 --> 00:00:07.517
Come on.

5
00:00:07.697 --> 00:00:09.757
See that telephone pole?
We'll take you, sir.

6
00:00:09.837 --> 00:00:10.737
Yeah.

7
00:00:10.817 --> 00:00:12.397
Yeah, we can take you.

8
00:00:12.477 --> 00:00:14.457
I can see if we got a pretty hard time.

9
00:00:14.537 --> 00:00:16.297
Well, I can touch on and take it.

10
00:00:16.377 --> 00:00:18.257
Yeah, come on. You want to try?

11
00:00:18.577 --> 00:00:19.577
Sure.

12
00:00:23.137 --> 00:00:24.257
Grab it up.

13
00:00:24.617 --> 00:00:26.057
Come on, man. Get ready.

14
00:00:53.997 --> 00:00:55.017
I'm sure I'm going to drive this.

15
00:00:55.097 --> 00:00:56.097
Watch me.

16
00:02:35.677 --> 00:02:38.917
Oh, my God.

17
00:03:36.717 --> 00:03:40.277
Sir, as high as this river is right now,
and with all the mud and sand it's

18
00:03:40.357 --> 00:03:43.177
carrying, they may never find that car.

19
00:03:56.237 --> 00:03:57.437
Right there.

20
00:03:58.037 --> 00:04:00.257
Alright, now let's hear your
story about how it happened.

21
00:04:00.337 --> 00:04:01.637
It wasn't our fault.

22
00:04:02.317 --> 00:04:03.317
Yeah,

23
00:04:03.717 --> 00:04:08.637
we were the first ones on the bridge and
coming along following the tracks and they

24
00:04:08.717 --> 00:04:12.557
wanted to get around us I guess they
lost control when they dropped off.

25
00:04:12.637 --> 00:04:14.696
I'm sure you didn't crowd them off.

26
00:04:28.677 --> 00:04:29.997
Three hours.

27
00:04:31.117 --> 00:04:33.977
Yeah, I'm sure I want
to find that car now.

28
00:04:34.157 --> 00:04:37.197
With this van and with that
current, we may never find it.

29
00:04:37.277 --> 00:04:39.806
Yeah, all I guess we
can do is keep trying.

30
00:05:07.397 --> 00:05:09.162
Come on, let's get down there.

31
00:05:30.017 --> 00:05:31.317
Mary Henry.

32
00:05:31.717 --> 00:05:33.197
Are you all right?

33
00:05:33.577 --> 00:05:35.037
How did you get out?

34
00:05:36.197 --> 00:05:38.785
Put this on. We better
get you back to town.

35
00:05:42.097 --> 00:05:44.637
What about the other girl.

36
00:05:47.737 --> 00:05:49.477
I don't know.

37
00:06:45.077 --> 00:06:47.137
Thank you.

38
00:08:25.177 --> 00:08:27.597
Is this like the one
I'll be playing in Utah?

39
00:08:27.677 --> 00:08:28.977
It's quite similar.

40
00:08:29.057 --> 00:08:31.577
I supervised the installation myself.

41
00:08:32.097 --> 00:08:34.317
The accident won't delay
your going, will it?

42
00:08:34.397 --> 00:08:35.397
No.

43
00:08:35.577 --> 00:08:37.157
I'm leaving this morning.

44
00:08:37.237 --> 00:08:38.817
There's nothing I can do in here.

45
00:08:38.897 --> 00:08:39.957
That's right.

46
00:08:40.217 --> 00:08:43.297
Well, Mary, you'll make a
fine organist for that church.

47
00:08:43.377 --> 00:08:45.617
It'll be very satisfying for you, I think.

48
00:08:45.697 --> 00:08:47.537
It's just a job to me.

49
00:08:47.717 --> 00:08:51.537
Well, it's not quite the attitude
for going into church work.

50
00:08:51.637 --> 00:08:52.937
I'm not taking the vows.

51
00:08:53.017 --> 00:08:54.257
I'm only going to play the organ.

52
00:08:54.337 --> 00:08:56.337
Oh, you want more than that?

53
00:08:56.417 --> 00:09:00.777
Of course, it doesn't pay much,
but, well, at least it's a start.

54
00:09:01.657 --> 00:09:04.245
Are you driving by
Benton to see your folks?

55
00:09:04.797 --> 00:09:06.217
No, I can't.

56
00:09:06.297 --> 00:09:07.877
I, I, I'm afraid.

57
00:09:07.957 --> 00:09:09.377
I, I, I forgot to leave.

58
00:09:09.457 --> 00:09:10.837
I try to say through.

59
00:09:12.037 --> 00:09:15.657
Mary, it takes more than
intellect to be a musician.

60
00:09:16.057 --> 00:09:18.377
Put your soul into it a little.

61
00:09:18.557 --> 00:09:19.557
OK?

62
00:09:26.117 --> 00:09:27.697
Good luck, Mary.

63
00:09:28.417 --> 00:09:30.997
Stop by and see us the
next time you're in.

64
00:09:31.077 --> 00:09:32.057
Thank you.

65
00:09:32.137 --> 00:09:34.157
But I'm never coming back.

66
00:09:47.457 --> 00:09:49.417
I don't know about that girl.

67
00:09:49.497 --> 00:09:50.717
How do you mean?

68
00:09:50.837 --> 00:09:54.237
The day before yesterday, she was the
only one of three girls to survive an

69
00:09:54.317 --> 00:09:55.317
accident.

70
00:09:55.597 --> 00:10:00.597
You'd think she'd feel a little
something like humbleness or gratitude.

71
00:10:01.117 --> 00:10:03.317
Never know what she thinks.

72
00:10:03.577 --> 00:10:05.977
She's always kept pretty much to herself.

73
00:10:06.057 --> 00:10:09.157
Yeah, and maybe in her
place I do the same thing.

74
00:10:09.457 --> 00:10:11.397
Just pick up life again.

75
00:10:11.677 --> 00:10:14.917
Well, she's so quiet like she fools you.

76
00:10:15.497 --> 00:10:17.977
But she's a tough-minded little thing.

77
00:10:18.057 --> 00:10:20.410
I guess that's what it takes to survive.

78
00:10:20.977 --> 00:10:24.437
But I still say she's behaving strangely.

79
00:10:24.757 --> 00:10:28.977
Well, if she's got a problem,
it'll go right along with her.

80
00:10:29.057 --> 00:10:30.057
Yep.

81
00:11:43.597 --> 00:11:45.137
Come on, boy.

82
00:15:06.457 --> 00:15:10.037
I help you fill it up all right.

83
00:15:35.717 --> 00:15:37.317
Anything else lady?

84
00:15:38.137 --> 00:15:42.797
Could you tell me what that big
structure is back a few miles by the lake?

85
00:15:42.937 --> 00:15:45.037
Oh, you mean the old bath house?

86
00:15:45.457 --> 00:15:48.437
That used to be a pretty
richy place in the old days.

87
00:15:48.517 --> 00:15:51.457
Then the lake went down and
they made a dance hall out of it.

88
00:15:51.537 --> 00:15:55.837
Then they put those buildings up out there
and made some sort of a carnival there

89
00:15:55.917 --> 00:15:56.917
for a while.

90
00:15:57.637 --> 00:15:59.277
That's years ago, though.

91
00:15:59.357 --> 00:16:01.037
Just stands out there now.

92
00:16:01.297 --> 00:16:02.417
I see.

93
00:16:05.897 --> 00:16:08.297
I have an address here of a rooming house.

94
00:16:08.377 --> 00:16:09.553
Could you direct me?

95
00:16:11.017 --> 00:16:14.370
Oh, sure. Well, that's just
right over here, little Wade.

96
00:16:23.137 --> 00:16:26.137
Been saving it for you
since I got your letter.

97
00:16:29.357 --> 00:16:31.717
Could have rented it
yesterday if it wanted.

98
00:16:31.797 --> 00:16:33.457
Oh, it's fine.

99
00:16:33.797 --> 00:16:35.697
It's just about what I expected.

100
00:16:35.777 --> 00:16:37.617
I knew you'd like it.

101
00:16:38.477 --> 00:16:41.257
There's ain't no regular
room in the house, you know.

102
00:16:41.337 --> 00:16:43.237
I only got you, Mr.

103
00:16:43.317 --> 00:16:45.017
Linden, across the hall.

104
00:16:50.717 --> 00:16:53.837
Each room's got its own
private bathroom, too.

105
00:16:56.897 --> 00:16:59.197
You can take all the baths you want.

106
00:16:59.277 --> 00:17:02.137
I'm not one to fuss
about things like that.

107
00:17:02.217 --> 00:17:04.864
Thank you. I think I'll
be quite comfortable.

108
00:17:05.077 --> 00:17:07.577
Well, hope you'll stay a while.

109
00:17:08.377 --> 00:17:11.777
I'm downstairs in the back
part of the house, so...

110
00:17:11.857 --> 00:17:16.151
If there's anything else you need,
I guess I'll have to wait for morning.

111
00:17:20.157 --> 00:17:21.217
Good night.

112
00:17:21.397 --> 00:17:23.217
Good night, Mrs. Calvary.

113
00:17:43.457 --> 00:17:45.217
Thank you.

114
00:18:41.797 --> 00:18:45.677
And this, Miss Henry,
is our pride and joy.

115
00:18:46.077 --> 00:18:49.057
You know this was made in the
same town where I've been studying.

116
00:18:49.137 --> 00:18:49.857
Of course.

117
00:18:49.937 --> 00:18:51.957
That's where we heard about you.

118
00:18:52.197 --> 00:18:55.037
Oh, by the way, you have
found a place to stay.

119
00:18:55.777 --> 00:18:56.777
Good.

120
00:18:57.157 --> 00:18:59.797
Well, we hope you're
going to like it here.

121
00:18:59.917 --> 00:19:04.137
We're not the largest church in this
area, of course, but we have a nice

122
00:19:04.217 --> 00:19:05.537
congregation.

123
00:19:06.557 --> 00:19:08.757
We'll have to have some sort of a section.

124
00:19:08.837 --> 00:19:11.977
They want to meet you.
Couldn't we just skip that?

125
00:19:12.057 --> 00:19:13.417
Skip that?

126
00:19:13.557 --> 00:19:16.657
I don't suppose it's
an absolute necessity.

127
00:19:16.737 --> 00:19:19.737
I don't know what some
of the ladies will say.

128
00:19:19.817 --> 00:19:22.697
If they say I'm a fine organist,
that should be enough, shouldn't it?

129
00:19:22.777 --> 00:19:24.237
Well,

130
00:19:24.557 --> 00:19:25.957
yes, of course.

131
00:19:26.037 --> 00:19:29.117
We'll let it go at
that for the time being.

132
00:19:29.197 --> 00:19:35.457
But, my dear, you cannot live
in isolation from the human race,

133
00:19:35.537 --> 00:19:36.537
you know.

134
00:19:37.077 --> 00:19:38.697
Mind if I try this now?

135
00:19:38.777 --> 00:19:40.037
I want you to.

136
00:20:02.297 --> 00:20:04.297
I'm I'm

137
00:20:30.677 --> 00:20:35.677
We have an organist capable stern tone.

138
00:22:01.097 --> 00:22:02.517
What do you see?

139
00:22:04.477 --> 00:22:05.417
Nothing.

140
00:22:05.497 --> 00:22:08.917
Nothing at all. I practiced all
afternoon and got me in the mood.

141
00:22:08.997 --> 00:22:10.617
You need some fresh air.

142
00:22:10.837 --> 00:22:13.237
I've got to make a call out past the lake.

143
00:22:13.317 --> 00:22:15.637
Would you like to come along for the ride?

144
00:22:15.717 --> 00:22:17.537
You know that old pavilion out there?

145
00:22:17.617 --> 00:22:18.617
Mm-hmm.

146
00:22:19.037 --> 00:22:21.057
Will we pass it? Go right by it.

147
00:22:21.137 --> 00:22:22.697
Stop and look at it if you like.

148
00:22:22.777 --> 00:22:24.757
I would with you along.

149
00:23:01.357 --> 00:23:03.537
This used to be quite a place.

150
00:23:03.717 --> 00:23:06.437
It's been deserted for a long time now.

151
00:23:06.517 --> 00:23:09.217
Will you take me in? My goodness, no.

152
00:23:09.297 --> 00:23:11.317
It isn't safe out there anymore.

153
00:23:11.417 --> 00:23:13.477
That's why they put up this barrier.

154
00:23:13.557 --> 00:23:15.917
It'd be very easy to step around it.

155
00:23:16.757 --> 00:23:20.477
What attraction could
there be for you out there?

156
00:23:20.597 --> 00:23:22.057
I'm not sure.

157
00:23:22.857 --> 00:23:25.017
reasonable person I don't know.

158
00:23:25.097 --> 00:23:30.197
Maybe I want to satisfy myself that the
place is nothing more than it appears to be.

159
00:23:30.577 --> 00:23:32.137
Would you take me out there?

160
00:23:32.217 --> 00:23:32.957
No.

161
00:23:33.037 --> 00:23:35.217
The law has placed it off limits.

162
00:23:35.297 --> 00:23:38.477
Wouldn't be very seemly for
a minister to break the law,

163
00:23:38.557 --> 00:23:40.037
would it? No.

164
00:23:40.437 --> 00:23:42.837
Maybe I can come back some other time.

165
00:23:44.177 --> 00:23:46.477
Shall we go along now?

166
00:24:13.137 --> 00:24:15.877
I thought that would be years big.

167
00:24:17.137 --> 00:24:18.477
That ought to be playing.

168
00:24:18.557 --> 00:24:21.337
It must take a long time.
You've been gone most a whole day.

169
00:24:21.417 --> 00:24:25.117
I went for a long drive in
the country with my new boss.

170
00:24:25.277 --> 00:24:27.377
An elderly minister.

171
00:24:28.897 --> 00:24:32.257
Oh, that must have
been a kick in the head.

172
00:24:33.357 --> 00:24:35.917
I learned that from the other boarder, Mr.

173
00:24:35.997 --> 00:24:36.997
Linden.

174
00:24:37.197 --> 00:24:38.737
Did you get some supper?

175
00:24:39.057 --> 00:24:40.417
Oh, I forgot.

176
00:24:40.497 --> 00:24:41.497
Uh,

177
00:24:41.697 --> 00:24:46.737
well, there's ain't no boarding house,
but I got some coffee and the sandwich

178
00:24:46.817 --> 00:24:50.077
makings left. I'll bring
you some up after a while.

179
00:24:50.157 --> 00:24:50.777
Good.

180
00:24:50.857 --> 00:24:53.777
I'll be taking one of those
battles you're so generous with.

181
00:24:53.857 --> 00:24:55.357
Well, take as many as you want.

182
00:24:55.437 --> 00:24:58.672
I ain't wanting to make a
fuss about a thing like that.

183
00:26:11.597 --> 00:26:13.538
I thought you were in the status.

184
00:26:14.417 --> 00:26:15.637
Yeah, I...

185
00:26:17.597 --> 00:26:19.877
I'm John Linden, I'm your
neighbor right across the hall.

186
00:26:19.957 --> 00:26:21.337
Oh, nice, please. We can excuse him.

187
00:26:21.417 --> 00:26:24.257
Hey, I... I was wondering
if you're not doing...

188
00:26:24.337 --> 00:26:25.984
I just... stand right there.

189
00:26:51.757 --> 00:26:57.857
I got him to do my stuff
I'm mad yeah I know I yeah

190
00:26:57.937 --> 00:27:04.277
yeah we I just thought you be
able to know that I think that

191
00:27:04.357 --> 00:27:10.317
you need it I thought that that's
very thoughtful but I can't I

192
00:27:10.397 --> 00:27:16.217
don't matter anything yet I don't know my

193
00:27:16.297 --> 00:27:22.377
dress right down the street like
a guy doesn't like to be fine so

194
00:27:22.457 --> 00:27:24.777
I made arrangements my room

195
00:27:35.357 --> 00:27:37.077
Good night, Mr. Lohman.

196
00:28:13.097 --> 00:28:14.997
I'm

197
00:28:16.977 --> 00:28:18.877
I'm

198
00:28:59.997 --> 00:29:01.517
Miss Henry?

199
00:29:01.777 --> 00:29:03.557
It's Miss Palmer.

200
00:29:21.797 --> 00:29:23.877
Who's the man in the hall?

201
00:29:27.517 --> 00:29:28.577
Oh,

202
00:29:29.757 --> 00:29:31.757
you must mean Mr. Linden.

203
00:29:31.837 --> 00:29:34.657
He has the room across the hall.

204
00:29:34.757 --> 00:29:35.757
No,

205
00:29:36.097 --> 00:29:37.817
I mean the other one.

206
00:29:38.117 --> 00:29:40.557
There is no other.

207
00:29:41.697 --> 00:29:43.397
Me and you and Mr.

208
00:29:43.477 --> 00:29:44.477
Linden.

209
00:29:44.737 --> 00:29:47.377
Us three is all there is, Miss Howe.

210
00:29:47.457 --> 00:29:49.751
But you must have passed him out there.

211
00:29:50.617 --> 00:29:52.637
You're needing this food.

212
00:29:53.377 --> 00:29:56.917
All the bats, Keaton,
makes you jumpy sometimes.

213
00:29:57.457 --> 00:30:00.617
Maybe you heard the
boards pop or something.

214
00:30:00.697 --> 00:30:03.057
These old houses creaked
worse than my knees.

215
00:30:03.137 --> 00:30:04.617
I didn't hear him, Mrs.

216
00:30:04.697 --> 00:30:05.217
Thomas.

217
00:30:05.297 --> 00:30:06.937
I saw him.

218
00:30:09.537 --> 00:30:11.657
Now, don't talk that way.

219
00:30:12.917 --> 00:30:15.357
I don't sleep so good as it is.

220
00:30:16.797 --> 00:30:19.397
These old houses, they...

221
00:30:19.477 --> 00:30:23.297
They're big enough so that you
could hide a man in every corner.

222
00:30:26.097 --> 00:30:29.777
You just gotta not let
your imagination run away.

223
00:30:29.857 --> 00:30:32.269
Are you going out there? Well, of course.

224
00:30:53.377 --> 00:30:55.337
There's nobody there.

225
00:30:57.867 --> 00:31:01.817
Now you just go and eat
that sandwich I made for you.

226
00:31:03.037 --> 00:31:06.857
Don't drink the coffee
if coffee keeps you awake.

227
00:31:06.937 --> 00:31:08.197
It won't.

228
00:31:11.457 --> 00:31:13.977
Coffee never keeps me awake.

229
00:32:36.837 --> 00:32:38.777
Well, good morning.

230
00:32:39.377 --> 00:32:41.457
I heard your alarm. I knew you'd be up.

231
00:32:41.537 --> 00:32:42.597
Guess what I got.

232
00:32:42.677 --> 00:32:44.357
I can't imagine.

233
00:32:44.457 --> 00:32:47.257
Just what it takes to
start the day off right.

234
00:32:47.337 --> 00:32:50.937
I'll make it in my room. You know, it saves
me having to go out and get dressed up.

235
00:32:51.017 --> 00:32:53.723
I had to get dressed to
come over here anyway.

236
00:32:54.277 --> 00:32:56.517
Oh, it looks just like what I need.

237
00:32:56.597 --> 00:33:00.337
Well, and two cups of coffee coming up.

238
00:33:05.097 --> 00:33:09.997
Hey, I guess you took her on last night
about me coming to your door and all.

239
00:33:10.077 --> 00:33:12.757
I'm not a very sociable
person over the now.

240
00:33:13.057 --> 00:33:15.417
How can I resist an inducement like this?

241
00:33:15.497 --> 00:33:16.497
What?

242
00:33:17.397 --> 00:33:19.297
Come on, I don't know all those big words.

243
00:33:19.377 --> 00:33:22.457
Just an ordinary guy works
in a warehouse, that's all.

244
00:33:22.537 --> 00:33:24.277
That's pretty good money, though.

245
00:33:24.357 --> 00:33:25.357
Hey,

246
00:33:25.717 --> 00:33:27.737
look, I got a couple of shots
left over from last night.

247
00:33:27.817 --> 00:33:29.641
You want a little bit in yours?

248
00:33:30.237 --> 00:33:33.337
It's not the recommended
breakfast for church organist.

249
00:33:33.417 --> 00:33:35.177
Oh, is that what you do?

250
00:33:35.477 --> 00:33:37.977
Hey, you mean they pay somebody
to play the organ in church?

251
00:33:38.057 --> 00:33:39.637
Some churches do.

252
00:33:40.737 --> 00:33:42.957
Hey, I hope you don't mind about this.

253
00:33:43.037 --> 00:33:44.917
I just didn't know you
were a church woman.

254
00:33:44.997 --> 00:33:47.585
To me, a church is just
a place of business.

255
00:33:48.097 --> 00:33:50.137
What a funny way to look at it.

256
00:33:50.217 --> 00:33:51.217
Why?

257
00:33:51.337 --> 00:33:55.757
People seem shocked because I took a job
in a church and I regard it simply as a

258
00:33:55.837 --> 00:33:56.677
job.

259
00:33:56.757 --> 00:34:00.228
I'm a professional organist
and I play for pay, that's all.

260
00:34:00.917 --> 00:34:03.799
Thinking like that,
don't I give you a nightmare?

261
00:34:05.457 --> 00:34:07.497
Strange, you should say that.

262
00:34:07.997 --> 00:34:09.757
As a matter of fact,

263
00:34:09.997 --> 00:34:15.137
not for that reason, mind you, but I
had the strangest feeling last night.

264
00:34:15.317 --> 00:34:16.317
Yeah,

265
00:34:16.697 --> 00:34:18.717
I had kind of a lost night myself.

266
00:34:19.017 --> 00:34:20.397
That's funny.

267
00:34:21.537 --> 00:34:24.397
The world is so different in the daylight.

268
00:34:25.197 --> 00:34:28.897
But in the dark your
fantasies get so out of hand.

269
00:34:29.757 --> 00:34:33.228
But in the daylight everything
falls back into place again.

270
00:34:35.377 --> 00:34:37.157
Let's have no more nights.

271
00:34:37.897 --> 00:34:41.037
Or let's make them more interesting.

272
00:34:44.197 --> 00:34:46.137
Hey, how did you get to
be at church all the day?

273
00:34:46.217 --> 00:34:47.797
I studied in college.

274
00:34:47.877 --> 00:34:49.777
I could have gone to college.

275
00:34:50.537 --> 00:34:53.777
Yeah, I used to play pretty good football,
but they wanted me to take a lot of

276
00:34:53.857 --> 00:34:55.297
classes and things, you know?

277
00:34:55.377 --> 00:34:56.597
Well, they're that way.

278
00:34:56.677 --> 00:34:59.057
Well, I'm just as smart as the next guy.

279
00:34:59.677 --> 00:35:01.697
Yeah, but I just didn't dig
with their teaching in school,

280
00:35:01.777 --> 00:35:06.297
you know? And the thing I hated
most was principal product.

281
00:35:07.217 --> 00:35:11.857
Principal product? You know,
like a principal product to Brazil.

282
00:35:15.937 --> 00:35:18.761
Coffee, beans, a snake
oil, you know, like that.

283
00:35:19.417 --> 00:35:21.777
Now that's cool, I couldn't care less.

284
00:35:21.857 --> 00:35:23.937
Now you know what I cared about was girls.

285
00:35:24.017 --> 00:35:26.077
Didn't they offer a course in that?

286
00:35:26.657 --> 00:35:29.598
If I would have done that,
I would have graduated.

287
00:35:30.997 --> 00:35:33.938
What's the matter? Can
you still taste the coffee?

288
00:35:34.197 --> 00:35:36.817
Come on, what do you
think, I'm an alcoholic?

289
00:35:36.897 --> 00:35:39.937
Look, I just like to start the
day off in a good mood, that's all.

290
00:35:40.017 --> 00:35:42.097
You must be hilarious by noon.

291
00:35:42.217 --> 00:35:45.117
Look, I'm just the kind
of a guy employed as one.

292
00:35:47.237 --> 00:35:50.117
Come on, come on. Did I
make your morning happy?

293
00:35:50.477 --> 00:35:53.117
This morning, you're
exactly what I needed.

294
00:35:53.397 --> 00:35:54.877
You're going to need
me in the evening, too.

295
00:35:54.957 --> 00:35:56.545
You just don't know it yet.

296
00:35:57.837 --> 00:35:59.537
I'll rinse off these cups.

297
00:35:59.617 --> 00:36:02.717
Oh, no, no, no. Just foils
of flavor for tomorrow.

298
00:36:03.337 --> 00:36:05.277
Thank you for the coffee.

299
00:36:05.357 --> 00:36:07.517
It was unsanitary, but delicious.

300
00:36:07.597 --> 00:36:12.197
Well, I should have put some
of the germ killer inside.

301
00:36:13.197 --> 00:36:15.957
Well, I take to leave early.

302
00:36:16.037 --> 00:36:18.277
I think you can get through the door.

303
00:36:19.037 --> 00:36:21.157
You know, you got the
wrong impression of me.

304
00:36:21.237 --> 00:36:24.097
Well, I meant because you
had so many things to carry.

305
00:36:24.177 --> 00:36:25.177
Oh.

306
00:36:25.657 --> 00:36:27.697
Like I said, I take to leave.

307
00:36:27.777 --> 00:36:29.137
Well, it's been a pleasure, Mr.

308
00:36:29.217 --> 00:36:31.697
Linden, but I'm sure
you have to get to work.

309
00:36:31.777 --> 00:36:32.577
Oh, don't you?

310
00:36:32.657 --> 00:36:35.277
No, I had the whole day free for shopping.

311
00:36:47.677 --> 00:36:49.717
Does the hem hang right in back?

312
00:36:49.797 --> 00:36:52.037
We might change the hemline a little.

313
00:36:52.137 --> 00:36:53.917
The drape is just fine.

314
00:36:53.997 --> 00:36:55.977
Otherwise, it looks very nice.

315
00:36:56.057 --> 00:37:00.137
I'm sure it isn't very chic to take
the second dress, but I like it.

316
00:37:00.217 --> 00:37:03.982
We altered a little here to make
it straight all the way around.

317
00:37:04.097 --> 00:37:07.156
There, do you want to go
back to your dressing room?

318
00:37:11.957 --> 00:37:15.097
Thank you.

319
00:37:49.737 --> 00:37:52.997
Thank you.

320
00:38:28.417 --> 00:38:31.677
I believe I have you deliver
the dress you don't mind.

321
00:38:32.677 --> 00:38:34.717
I did say I paid.

322
00:38:50.637 --> 00:38:52.537
What's the matter with it?

323
00:38:56.217 --> 00:38:58.137
What's the matter with everyone?

324
00:39:01.457 --> 00:39:03.377
Why don't they answer me?

325
00:39:29.217 --> 00:39:31.637
Thank you.

326
00:41:00.137 --> 00:41:02.497
What is it? That man.

327
00:41:03.877 --> 00:41:05.597
I didn't mean any harm.

328
00:41:05.677 --> 00:41:07.442
I just stopped to get a drink.

329
00:41:07.717 --> 00:41:08.717
No.

330
00:41:09.637 --> 00:41:10.537
No.

331
00:41:10.617 --> 00:41:12.617
It was that man.

332
00:41:13.957 --> 00:41:15.497
That man.

333
00:41:17.677 --> 00:41:19.717
There was someone else there.

334
00:41:19.797 --> 00:41:21.597
That strange man was there.

335
00:41:21.677 --> 00:41:23.897
Now look, look. You've had a fright.

336
00:41:24.037 --> 00:41:25.677
Hysteria won't solve anything.

337
00:41:25.757 --> 00:41:27.117
Now control yourself.

338
00:41:27.197 --> 00:41:29.197
Look, I'm Dr. Samuel.

339
00:41:29.777 --> 00:41:32.437
My office is right
across the street there.

340
00:41:32.837 --> 00:41:34.377
You've had a shock.

341
00:41:35.137 --> 00:41:38.117
If you would like my assistance,
I'll be glad to offer it.

342
00:41:38.197 --> 00:41:39.297
Thank you.

343
00:41:39.597 --> 00:41:40.857
Could I come with you now?

344
00:41:40.937 --> 00:41:41.937
Certainly.

345
00:41:42.137 --> 00:41:43.777
I'll take her over to my office.

346
00:41:43.857 --> 00:41:45.681
We'll see that she's all right.

347
00:42:00.197 --> 00:42:03.777
It was more than just not
being able to hear anything.

348
00:42:04.597 --> 00:42:06.957
Or make contact with anyone.

349
00:42:07.217 --> 00:42:09.277
It was as though...

350
00:42:10.877 --> 00:42:13.677
As though for a time I didn't exist.

351
00:42:15.217 --> 00:42:17.897
As though I had no place in the world.

352
00:42:18.877 --> 00:42:21.237
No part of the life around me.

353
00:42:22.257 --> 00:42:24.177
And then you saw this...

354
00:42:24.257 --> 00:42:25.937
this man?

355
00:42:26.897 --> 00:42:27.897
Yes.

356
00:42:30.697 --> 00:42:34.457
You'll excuse my back, but I wanted
to get some of that written down.

357
00:42:34.537 --> 00:42:36.977
I must have been talking for an hour.

358
00:42:37.057 --> 00:42:40.317
Anything else? Anything
you haven't told me?

359
00:42:41.017 --> 00:42:42.537
That's all there is.

360
00:42:42.857 --> 00:42:44.377
That's the whole story.

361
00:42:44.457 --> 00:42:45.857
He's been following me.

362
00:42:45.937 --> 00:42:46.997
That's all there is to it.

363
00:42:47.077 --> 00:42:49.597
It isn't that simple, Bo, is it?

364
00:42:51.337 --> 00:42:54.497
He could hardly have been in a park this
afternoon, or one of us men would have seen

365
00:42:54.577 --> 00:42:55.457
him.

366
00:42:55.537 --> 00:42:58.737
And that night in the hallway, you said
yourself that landlady came up a minute

367
00:42:58.817 --> 00:43:01.111
later, and she didn't see him, did she?

368
00:43:01.377 --> 00:43:03.157
What are you driving at?

369
00:43:03.337 --> 00:43:07.157
It's been less than a week since you
were in a car that crashed into the river.

370
00:43:07.237 --> 00:43:09.697
How you got out of that,
no one seems to know.

371
00:43:09.777 --> 00:43:12.977
But that experience must have
been a serious emotional shock.

372
00:43:13.057 --> 00:43:15.137
You think I imagined all of it, don't you?

373
00:43:15.217 --> 00:43:17.217
You think I'm insane? I didn't say that.

374
00:43:17.297 --> 00:43:20.437
I don't mean that. I'm a competent person.

375
00:43:20.737 --> 00:43:24.237
Anything, I'm a realist. I'm
not given to imagining anything.

376
00:43:24.317 --> 00:43:25.317
Hardwash.

377
00:43:25.837 --> 00:43:27.957
All of us imagine things.

378
00:43:28.437 --> 00:43:31.657
Have you never heard two men talking behind
your back and imagined they were talking

379
00:43:31.737 --> 00:43:32.797
about you?

380
00:43:34.117 --> 00:43:37.217
Have you never imagined you saw someone
you knew and walked up to them and found

381
00:43:37.297 --> 00:43:38.737
they were a perfect stranger?

382
00:43:38.817 --> 00:43:40.877
I don't see what this has to do with it.

383
00:43:40.957 --> 00:43:42.317
The point is this.

384
00:43:42.397 --> 00:43:44.637
Our imaginations play tricks on it.

385
00:43:44.717 --> 00:43:47.177
They often misinterpret
what we see and hear.

386
00:43:47.257 --> 00:43:48.377
Do you agree?

387
00:43:48.657 --> 00:43:50.277
I suppose so.

388
00:43:50.737 --> 00:43:54.237
If that can happen in ordinary
times, go a step further.

389
00:43:54.317 --> 00:43:58.697
Look what can happen in a high fever
or following a serious emotional shock.

390
00:43:58.777 --> 00:44:02.424
It doesn't seem possible that
I could have imagined all of it.

391
00:44:02.557 --> 00:44:06.557
Does this man, this figure,
resemble anyone you've ever known?

392
00:44:06.637 --> 00:44:08.277
An acquaintance? Or your father?

393
00:44:08.357 --> 00:44:09.077
No.

394
00:44:09.157 --> 00:44:10.857
You have a boyfriend here or back home?

395
00:44:10.937 --> 00:44:12.837
No, and I have no desire for one.

396
00:44:12.917 --> 00:44:13.917
Never?

397
00:44:14.137 --> 00:44:15.157
No.

398
00:44:16.277 --> 00:44:19.097
I'm surprised to find myself saying that.

399
00:44:19.177 --> 00:44:20.737
But it's true.

400
00:44:21.057 --> 00:44:24.857
I have no desire for the
close company of other people.

401
00:44:24.937 --> 00:44:26.837
Have you always felt this way?

402
00:44:29.037 --> 00:44:30.797
I don't know.

403
00:44:30.877 --> 00:44:33.417
Don't you want to join in the
things that other people do?

404
00:44:33.497 --> 00:44:35.257
Share the experiences of other people?

405
00:44:35.337 --> 00:44:38.497
I don't think capable of
being very close to people.

406
00:44:38.937 --> 00:44:43.157
I do feel that perhaps I'm trying
to reach out for those other things.

407
00:44:43.237 --> 00:44:45.157
Do you feel guilty wanting them?

408
00:44:46.217 --> 00:44:47.777
I don't understand you.

409
00:44:47.857 --> 00:44:53.537
I'm not a psychiatrist and perhaps I'm
being clumsy at all this but I am suggesting

410
00:44:53.617 --> 00:44:56.157
that perhaps this figure
represents a guilt feeling.

411
00:44:56.237 --> 00:44:57.497
Oh that's ridiculous.

412
00:44:58.237 --> 00:44:59.237
Maybe.

413
00:44:59.377 --> 00:45:01.037
Frankly I don't know.

414
00:45:01.977 --> 00:45:03.877
Well I know one thing.

415
00:45:04.357 --> 00:45:07.317
My imagination is playing tricks on me.

416
00:45:07.397 --> 00:45:08.897
I'm going to put a stop to it.

417
00:45:08.977 --> 00:45:11.683
You're a very strong
willed person aren't you?

418
00:45:11.837 --> 00:45:14.057
I survived that's what you mean.

419
00:45:14.377 --> 00:45:16.897
That old pavilion out by the

420
00:45:17.877 --> 00:45:20.818
Somehow you associate it
with all this, don't you?

421
00:45:21.197 --> 00:45:22.917
I could go out there.

422
00:45:23.757 --> 00:45:25.857
I could put an end to that, too.

423
00:45:26.597 --> 00:45:29.137
I could go out there. Now, don't be hasty.

424
00:45:29.997 --> 00:45:34.357
If it is all my imagination,
I could put a stop to it.

425
00:45:34.437 --> 00:45:36.557
Maybe, but at least
someone should be with you.

426
00:45:36.637 --> 00:45:37.857
Now, I can't possibly get away now.

427
00:45:37.937 --> 00:45:40.757
As you say, Doctor, I'm
a person of strong will.

428
00:45:40.837 --> 00:45:43.237
And the time to go out there is now.

429
00:45:43.537 --> 00:45:47.057
And if I have to, I can go alone.

430
00:46:48.057 --> 00:46:50.617
I'm sorry.

431
00:48:00.317 --> 00:48:01.477
Thank you.

432
00:48:28.157 --> 00:48:31.457
Thank you.

433
00:50:17.777 --> 00:50:20.377
Say, I don't want to
get turned down again.

434
00:50:20.897 --> 00:50:23.497
I was thinking asking you out to dinner.

435
00:50:23.637 --> 00:50:25.877
I stopped for a bite to eat on the way in.

436
00:50:25.957 --> 00:50:27.777
Anyway, I have to practice at the church.

437
00:50:27.857 --> 00:50:28.857
Look,

438
00:50:29.917 --> 00:50:31.497
I was about to fight.

439
00:50:31.637 --> 00:50:35.257
To go someplace and dance or something.

440
00:50:35.337 --> 00:50:36.317
I'm sorry.

441
00:50:36.397 --> 00:50:38.177
I'm not much for dancing.

442
00:50:42.137 --> 00:50:45.097
Hey, you mind if I ask you a question?

443
00:50:46.017 --> 00:50:49.157
until I get it. What,
are you afraid of men?

444
00:50:49.237 --> 00:50:51.597
No, I'm not afraid of men.

445
00:50:51.677 --> 00:50:52.957
Ah, well.

446
00:50:53.637 --> 00:50:55.617
You seem sort of cold.

447
00:50:56.557 --> 00:50:58.837
This morning when I
brought you the coffee.

448
00:50:58.917 --> 00:50:59.857
Friendly.

449
00:50:59.937 --> 00:51:02.077
This morning I needed company.

450
00:51:03.017 --> 00:51:05.737
Well, maybe you'll need company tonight.

451
00:51:06.677 --> 00:51:08.697
Better than walking home alone.

452
00:51:10.257 --> 00:51:11.317
Yes.

453
00:51:11.717 --> 00:51:13.037
It is.

454
00:51:13.897 --> 00:51:15.937
I should be finished around nine.

455
00:51:16.017 --> 00:51:19.297
Would that be all right? It's okay by me.

456
00:51:22.257 --> 00:51:24.217
Say, see you in church.

457
00:51:50.677 --> 00:51:53.157
Thank you.

458
00:52:20.597 --> 00:52:23.377
Thank you.

459
00:53:26.857 --> 00:53:27.857
Let's go.

460
00:54:50.797 --> 00:54:52.557
Propheal! Sacrilege!

461
00:54:52.637 --> 00:54:55.057
What are you playing in this church?

462
00:54:55.297 --> 00:54:57.397
Have you no respect?

463
00:54:57.477 --> 00:54:59.777
Do you feel no reverence?

464
00:55:00.597 --> 00:55:05.017
And I feel sorry for you
and your lack of soul.

465
00:55:05.297 --> 00:55:10.677
This organ, the music of this church,
these things have meaning and significance to

466
00:55:10.757 --> 00:55:11.277
us.

467
00:55:11.357 --> 00:55:13.897
I assume they did to you.

468
00:55:14.357 --> 00:55:20.457
But without this awareness, I'm
afraid you cannot be our organist.

469
00:55:20.537 --> 00:55:24.137
In conscience, I must ask you to resign.

470
00:55:33.317 --> 00:55:34.757
I'm here.

471
00:55:48.297 --> 00:55:51.157
That does not mean
that I'm abandoning you.

472
00:55:51.237 --> 00:55:53.825
Nor should you turn
your back on the church.

473
00:55:54.557 --> 00:55:56.697
and I urge you to accept it.

474
00:56:26.917 --> 00:56:28.097
Well, hi there.

475
00:56:28.177 --> 00:56:30.137
I've been waiting an
awful long time for you.

476
00:56:30.217 --> 00:56:33.746
My car's just over there.
I know just the right place to go.

477
00:56:57.637 --> 00:56:59.777
What's the matter, don't you drink either?

478
00:56:59.857 --> 00:57:01.117
Not really.

479
00:57:01.197 --> 00:57:02.197
Not really.

480
00:57:02.937 --> 00:57:04.777
What's this there if
you don't drink really?

481
00:57:04.857 --> 00:57:05.897
Answer me that.

482
00:57:06.897 --> 00:57:12.837
Now me, I not only drink
really, I really drink.

483
00:57:18.297 --> 00:57:20.897
What's the matter,
do you like the music either?

484
00:57:20.977 --> 00:57:23.437
I like it fine. You don't like it.

485
00:57:23.517 --> 00:57:27.977
You don't like to dance
and you don't like to drink.

486
00:57:28.357 --> 00:57:30.757
You don't like for a
man to hold you close.

487
00:57:30.837 --> 00:57:31.837
That's it, isn't it?

488
00:57:31.917 --> 00:57:33.337
I didn't say that.

489
00:57:33.417 --> 00:57:35.652
You haven't said anything all evening.

490
00:57:38.377 --> 00:57:40.077
Why don't I go play that song again?

491
00:57:40.157 --> 00:57:41.777
You like it so much.

492
00:57:47.577 --> 00:57:50.037
Hey, Johnny, who's the doll?

493
00:57:50.597 --> 00:57:51.997
Nobody you know, Chippen.

494
00:57:52.077 --> 00:57:54.577
Come on now you've been holding out on me.

495
00:57:54.657 --> 00:57:57.598
That's not the kind of
pig you usually drag around

496
00:57:58.077 --> 00:57:59.757
You quit licking your chops.

497
00:57:59.837 --> 00:58:01.237
She's out of your class

498
00:58:01.457 --> 00:58:02.917
You want a bet?

499
00:58:04.077 --> 00:58:05.597
Lay off, huh?

500
00:58:06.737 --> 00:58:08.597
I got something on the stove there man.

501
00:58:08.677 --> 00:58:10.237
Listen, I'll help you put it over.

502
00:58:10.317 --> 00:58:13.497
I don't want her to think
I even know creeps like you

503
00:58:15.217 --> 00:58:16.457
Good luck

504
00:58:24.457 --> 00:58:28.097
He's a college fellow.

505
00:58:29.597 --> 00:58:31.437
He told me about this girl.

506
00:58:31.517 --> 00:58:32.977
He wanted to meet me.

507
00:58:34.357 --> 00:58:35.857
He wanted me to meet her.

508
00:58:35.937 --> 00:58:37.537
What are you telling me?

509
00:58:37.997 --> 00:58:39.777
I said, how could I?

510
00:58:39.857 --> 00:58:41.437
You're my date, you know.

511
00:58:45.897 --> 00:58:47.437
He said, you were...

512
00:58:47.697 --> 00:58:50.477
Didn't seem to enjoy my company much.

513
00:58:50.557 --> 00:58:52.057
That's not true.

514
00:58:52.477 --> 00:58:55.617
I really appreciate you
taking me out this evening.

515
00:58:55.997 --> 00:58:58.537
I've had a miserable night if you haven't.

516
00:59:00.357 --> 00:59:01.817
Forget it. Come on. Here.

517
00:59:01.897 --> 00:59:03.457
Join a party. Drink up.

518
00:59:09.377 --> 00:59:10.977
